course: dictionary
lesson: 4019
title: Gastric: all about the stomach
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Gastric is an adjective. It tells you something is about the stomach. Look at the sentence «The gastric-brooding frog of Australia raised its babies in its stomach, but it is now extinct.» The word stomach is right there, so gastric must be linked to the stomach.
explain: Try the swap check. Put "stomach" in place of gastric: "the stomach-brooding frog" still makes sense, so your meaning is right. Notice the hyphen in gastric-brooding: it joins two words so they work together as one describing word.
explain: Doctors and scientists use gastric often. A gastric bug is an illness that affects your stomach and gut, and it can make you feel sick and have diarrhoea. Gastric juice is the liquid in your stomach that helps break down your food.
fact: Gastric means about the stomach.
fact: Gastric juice in the stomach contains acid that helps break down food.
fact: A gastric bug, or gastric flu, is an illness of the stomach and gut, often with sickness and diarrhoea.
fact: In medicine, gastric appears in words like gastric ulcer.
fact: «Gastric juice», «gastric bug» and «gastric pain» are common phrases.
exercise: «The gastric-brooding frog of Australia raised its babies in its stomach.» What does gastric mean here? | About the feet | *About the stomach | About the eyes | About the heart
exercise: The nurse says Sam has a gastric bug. What is a gastric bug? | *An illness of the stomach and gut, often with sickness | A loud noise in the ear | A tiny insect that bites at night | A bug that lives in a computer
exercise: What does gastric juice help your body do? | Grow taller | *Break down food | Keep you warm | Help you hear
test: «Gastric pain» means pain in which part of the body? | *Your stomach | Your legs | Your head | Your hands
test: Which word means about the stomach? | Cardiac | *Gastric | Nasal | Dermal
exam: Read «The gastric-brooding frog of Australia raised its babies in its stomach, but it is now extinct.» What does gastric mean? | *About the stomach | About the skin | About the lungs | About the brain
